From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:44:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] ASoC: nexell: add S5P6818/S5P4418 I2S driver

Port the Nexell I2S controller (a variant of the Samsung I2S with
CON/CSR/FIC/TXD/RXD registers, so mainline samsung/i2s.c does not apply)
to a modern ASoC CPU DAI. Data movement uses the generic dmaengine PCM
over the ARM PL080 DMA, replacing the vendor's private PCM component.
Master mode, MCLK out to the codec, 256/384 fs. Enabled via
SND_SOC_NEXELL / SND_SOC_NEXELL_I2S and wired into sound/soc.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
